      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel skeptical when seeking help, especially when deep exhaustion overshadows hope. Feeling perpetually tired of existing is a profound form of emotional pain, and it deserves real attention beyond just a crisis call. Perhaps instead of general outreach, you could look into finding a therapist who specializes in existential distress or chronic loneliness. They can help you explore these deep feelings in a space designed for deeper understanding rather than just immediate crisis management.",
